# routes that are not operations of the document: 5
DELETE  /mcp  The end of an MCP session, not an API operation; it authenticates itself with a bearer token (D109 D-1).
GET     /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource  OAuth protected-resource metadata (RFC 9728) for the MCP server: a client reads it before it has a credential, so it is public by design.
GET     /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp  The same document at the path RFC 9728 derives from the resource `/mcp`: public by design.
GET     /mcp  The MCP endpoint's stream, not an API operation; it authenticates itself with a bearer token (D109 D-1).
POST    /mcp  The MCP endpoint speaks the protocol of docs/mcp-tools.md, not an API operation; it is public to the guard and authenticates itself with a bearer token (D109 D-1).
